 "plain_statement": "JOINS: 200 candidates (100 cross-collection, listed first; central expected real 0.09 cross vs 0.71 same). Among gallery pairs that look like these, 30% are known joins on average (out-of-fold calibration, AUC 0.858), but the gallery was built around known joins, so a pair that is NOT already known is far less likely to be one: we expect about 0.8 real new joins in the 200 (range 0.27-2.66 for 0.1-1.0 undiscovered partners per fragment; x0.59 = 0.47 after the hide-one-source check, in which the procedure found 35 hidden PGP joins vs 29.67 predicted and 25 hidden FJP joins vs 72.47 predicted). In other words: expect zero to a few real joins; the list is a calibrated review queue, not a set of finds. SCRIBES: leave-one-out accuracy over 22 scribes (qwen3vl-vit512-heb-v22b-step1200: centroid 0.349, 1-NN 0.457, held-out 0.1166; fusion: centroid 0.401, 1-NN 0.387, held-out 0.3067); candidates use dinov2-base__masked+dinov2-base__mpatches+qwen3vl-vit512-heb-v22b-step1200__masked. At margin >= 0.0243 LOO precision is 0.80 at 9% coverage in-sample (the threshold was picked there); nested cross-validation gives 0.7255 at 10% coverage. 59 of 1337 unlabelled documentary fragments clear it (6 others were left out because a known join or shared PGP document already ties them to a labelled fragment), 5 fall outside the proposed scribe's PGP dates, 54 are listed. 13 of those go to scribes who are alone in their period (meir-ben-naim, yosef-b-meir-somekh-ha-kohen); for them a matching date shows the period, not the hand. For the other 44 the date check gives error 1.0 and about 0.0 correct (95% range (0.0, 25.4), from only 6 dated). Over all 54: about 27.7 correct by dates, 21.6 by the open-set moments estimate; both are optimistic for period- or script-isolated scribes. The 0.8 LOO precision does NOT carry over to unlabelled documents. The v22b tower alone is not usable for attribution: 78 of its 84 confident picks go to mikhail-b-abd-al-masih, and 11 of 12 dated picks are outside the proposed scribe's dates.",
 "notes": [
  "p_labelled / band_labelled = share of gallery pairs with the same similarity/rank/cross profile that are KNOWN joins (isotonic-calibrated, out-of-fold by known-join component); p_discovery_est = rho * p/(1-p), the base-rate-corrected chance that a NOT-known pair is a join.",
  "rho (undiscovered-to-known join ratio in the gallery) is an assumption: gallery 5,176 of ~400k Genizah fragments; the hide-one-source validation checks the odds transfer itself, not rho.",
  "cross_collection uses holding_key() on the canonical id; the manifest collection strings split one holding into several spellings, which inflates eval_images' cross-collection counts (315 vs 266 queries).",
  "Discovery yield is limited by gallery coverage: an undiscovered partner is in this 5k gallery ~1.3% of the time. Extracting the same fused features for all 54k imaged fragments is the main lever for real join discovery.",
  "Scribe candidates are fragments with PGP documentary records and no PGP scribe relation; exemplars are the nearest labelled fragments of the proposed scribe (same-document pairs never used)."
 ]
